From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a native ARM64 child's images live in the JIT pool

A native ARM64 child (0249) runs each image from its JIT-pool copy, but
NtMapViewOfSection returned the PE view, so the PEB, the module list and
every RVA a program computes from its own code addresses (ADRP, pool
addresses) against its module base disagreed by the distance between
the two. World of Warcraft's ARM64 client failed its start-up checks on
it ("Game Initialization Failed").

Decision 0176: for such a child, virtual_map_image returns the pool copy
as the image (all images but its private ntdll, which the unix side
writes through its view). The copy holds the whole image and its header's
ImageBase is the copy's address. The view stays as Wine's and the
server's backing store: NtQueryVirtualMemory (basic and image
information), NtProtectVirtualMemory and NtUnmapViewOfSection take the
copy's addresses and answer in them, the IAT sync never copies the view
over a presented copy, an exception in one keeps its pool pc, and the
PE-side ntdll's reverse translation (the unwinder, resources) leaves its
addresses alone. x86-64 and ARM64EC processes are unchanged.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
